    {
      "@id": "concept:aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016-sch-1-sec-70",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "70 Definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016#sch-1-sec-70"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016.pdf, p.25",
      "values:originalText": "In this Part:\ncommencement time means the time when this Part commences.\nnew law means the Aged Care Act 1997 as in force immediately after\nthe commencement time.\nold law means the Aged Care Act 1997 as in force immediately before\nthe commencement time.",
      "skos:definition": "In this Part:\ncommencement time means the time when this Part commences.\nnew law means the Aged Care Act 1997 as in force immediately after\nthe commencement time.\nold law means the Aged Care Act 1997 as in force immediately before\nthe commencement time.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016-sch-1-sec-70-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7ebd67b0f598b1f5e2bcace3280a88ac540c99c39b4379972881f559e9fab26b",
      "skos:note": "Defines terms for this Part"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016#sch-1-sec-70",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "70 Definitions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 25,
      "values:originalText": "In this Part:\ncommencement time means the time when this Part commences.\nnew law means the Aged Care Act 1997 as in force immediately after\nthe commencement time.\nold law means the Aged Care Act 1997 as in force immediately before\nthe commencement time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016-sch-1-sec-70-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016-sch-1-sec-70"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016-sch-1-sec-71",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "71 Amendments relating to approval of providers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016#sch-1-sec-71"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016.pdf, p.25",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendments of sections 8-1 and 8-5 of the Aged Care Act 1997\nmade by this Schedule apply in relation to any application to be\napproved as a provider of aged care:\n\n(a) made after the commencement time; or\n\n(b) made, but not determined, before the commencement time.\n(2)\nThe amendments of subsection 8-3(1) of the Aged Care Act 1997 made\nby this Schedule apply in relation to:\n\n(a) any application to be approved as a provider of aged care\nmade after the commencement time; and\n\n(b) any change of circumstances referred to in\nparagraph 9-1(1)(a) of that Act that occurs after the\ncommencement time; and\n\n(c) any request made to an approved provider under\nsubsection 9-2(1) or paragraph 9-3B(2)(a) of that Act after\nthe commencement time; and\n\n(d) any approval revoked under paragraph 10-3(1)(b) of that Act\nafter the commencement time.\n(3)\nIf:\n\n(a) a person has, before the commencement time, been approved\nunder section 8-1 of the Aged Care Act 1997 as a provider of\naged care; and\n\n(b) at the commencement time:\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThe amendments of sections 8-1 and 8-5 of the Aged Care Act 1997\nmade by this Schedule apply in relation to any application to be\napproved as a provider of aged care:\n\n(a) made after the commencement time; or\n\n(b) made, but not determined, before the commencement time.\n(2)\nThe amendments of subsection 8-3(1) of the Aged Care Act 1997 made\nby this Schedule apply in relation to:\n\n(a) any application to be approved as a provider of aged care\nmade after the commencement time; and\n\n(b) any change of circumstances referred to in\nparagraph 9-1(1)(a) of that Act that occurs after the\ncommencement time; and\n\n(c) any request made to an approved provider under\nsubsection 9-2(1) or paragraph 9-3B(2)(a) of that Act after\nthe commencement time; and\n\n(d) any approval revoked under paragraph 10-3(1)(b) of that Act\nafter the commencement time.\n(3)\nIf:\n\n(a) a person has, before the commencement time, been approved\nunder section 8-1 of the Aged Care Act 1997 as a provider of\naged care; and\n\n(b) at the commencement time:\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016-sch-1-sec-71-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016-sch-1-sec-71-logic-alleninterval-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a9f40ccb5d575ed7d82019263f33399d9d2e2864ab0c4ca3a9397739d2bb557d",
      "skos:note": "Amendments apply to applications made after or before the commencement time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016#sch-1-sec-71",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "71 Amendments relating to approval of providers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 25,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendments of sections 8-1 and 8-5 of the Aged Care Act 1997\nmade by this Schedule apply in relation to any application to be\napproved as a provider of aged care:\n\n(a) made after the commencement time; or\n\n(b) made, but not determined, before the commencement time.\n(2)\nThe amendments of subsection 8-3(1) of the Aged Care Act 1997 made\nby this Schedule apply in relation to:\n\n(a) any application to be approved as a provider of aged care\nmade after the commencement time; and\n\n(b) any change of circumstances referred to in\nparagraph 9-1(1)(a) of that Act that occurs after the\ncommencement time; and\n\n(c) any request made to an approved provider under\nsubsection 9-2(1) or paragraph 9-3B(2)(a) of that Act after\nthe commencement time; and\n\n(d) any approval revoked under paragraph 10-3(1)(b) of that Act\nafter the commencement time.\n(3)\nIf:\n\n(a) a person has, before the commencement time, been approved\nunder section 8-1 of the Aged Care Act 1997 as a provider of\naged care; and\n\n(b) at the commencement time:\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016-sch-1-sec-71-norm",
