    {
      "@id": "concept:aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016-sch-1-sec-74",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "74 Applications relating to allocations of home care places",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016#sch-1-sec-74"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nIf:\n\n(a) a person has, before the commencement time, made an\napplication under section 13-1 of the Aged Care Act 1997 for\nan allocation of places in respect of home care subsidy; and\n\n(b) the Secretary has not, before the commencement time,\nnotified the person under section 14-8 of that Act in relation\nto the application;\nthe application is taken never to have been made.\n(2)\nIf:\n\n(a) a person has, before the commencement time, made an\napplication under section 16-2, 16-7, 17-2 or 17-7 of the\nAged Care Act 1997 relating to a place in respect of home\ncare subsidy; and\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nApplication and transitional provisions  Part 3\n\nNo. 19, 2016\nAged Care Legislation Amendment (Increasing Consumer Choice) Act\n\n(b) the Secretary has not, before the commencement time, given\nnotice under section 16-5, 16-7, 17-5 or 17-7 of that Act (as\nthe case may be) in relation to the application;\nthe application is taken never to have been made.",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nIf:\n\n(a) a person has, before the commencement time, made an\napplication under section 13-1 of the Aged Care Act 1997 for\nan allocation of places in respect of home care subsidy; and\n\n(b) the Secretary has not, before the commencement time,\nnotified the person under section 14-8 of that Act in relation\nto the application;\nthe application is taken never to have been made.\n(2)\nIf:\n\n(a) a person has, before the commencement time, made an\napplication under section 16-2, 16-7, 17-2 or 17-7 of the\nAged Care Act 1997 relating to a place in respect of home\ncare subsidy; and\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nApplication and transitional provisions  Part 3\n\nNo. 19, 2016\nAged Care Legislation Amendment (Increasing Consumer Choice) Act\n\n(b) the Secretary has not, before the commencement time, given\nnotice under section 16-5, 16-7, 17-5 or 17-7 of that Act (as\nthe case may be) in relation to the application;\nthe application is taken never to have been made.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016-sch-1-sec-74-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016-sch-1-sec-74-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a932f0c3b37ccba4c8066e03df4e4f075e4f545f75e7212df02bb0a06746414b",
      "skos:note": "Application for home care subsidy is taken never to have been made if certain conditions are not met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016#sch-1-sec-74",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "74 Applications relating to allocations of home care places",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nIf:\n\n(a) a person has, before the commencement time, made an\napplication under section 13-1 of the Aged Care Act 1997 for\nan allocation of places in respect of home care subsidy; and\n\n(b) the Secretary has not, before the commencement time,\nnotified the person under section 14-8 of that Act in relation\nto the application;\nthe application is taken never to have been made.\n(2)\nIf:\n\n(a) a person has, before the commencement time, made an\napplication under section 16-2, 16-7, 17-2 or 17-7 of the\nAged Care Act 1997 relating to a place in respect of home\ncare subsidy; and\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nApplication and transitional provisions  Part 3\n\nNo. 19, 2016\nAged Care Legislation Amendment (Increasing Consumer Choice) Act\n\n(b) the Secretary has not, before the commencement time, given\nnotice under section 16-5, 16-7, 17-5 or 17-7 of that Act (as\nthe case may be) in relation to the application;\nthe application is taken never to have been made."
    },
