      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) during the relevant day there is in force a home care agreement under which a care recipient, approved under section 46-1 of the Aged Care Act 1997 or section 46-1 of the Aged Care (Transitional Provisions) Act 1997, for home care subsidy",
      "cml:conclusionText": "There must be an allocation of a place for home care subsidy under Part 2.2 of the Aged Care Act 1997"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016-sch-1-sec-78-logic-alleninterval-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": ">=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must have been allocated a place for home care subsidy on or before the relevant day",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) during the relevant day the approved provider holds an allocation of a place for home care subsidy that is in force under Part 2.2 of the Aged Care Act 1997;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The approved provider must have been allocated a place for home care subsidy on or before the relevant day"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016-sch-1-sec-78-logic-ltl-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "<=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must not have ceased allocation of place for home care subsidy by the relevant day",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) during the relevant day the approved provider holds an allocation of a place for home care subsidy that is in force under Part 2.2 of the Aged Care Act 1997;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The approved provider must not have ceased allocation of a place for home care subsidy by the relevant day"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016-sch-1-sec-78-logic-deontic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "must provide",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must provide evidence of allocation of place for home care subsidy under Part 2.2 of the Aged Care Act 1997",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) during the relevant day the approved provider holds an allocation of a place for home care subsidy that is in force under Part 2.2 of the Aged Care Act 1997;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The approved provider must provide evidence of allocation of a place for home care subsidy under Part 2.2 of the Aged Care Act 1997"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016-sch-1-sec-79",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "79 Unspent home care amount",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016#sch-1-sec-79"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nParagraph 46-1(1)(f) of the Aged Care Act 1997 and the Aged Care\n(Transitional Provisions) Act 1997, as inserted by this Schedule, applies\nin relation to any unspent home care amount that relates to home care\nsubsidy, and home care fees, that were or are payable in respect of\n1 July 2015 or any later day.\n(2)\nSubsection 95-1(3) of the Aged Care Act 1997, as inserted by this\nSchedule, applies in relation to any Commonwealth portion of unspent\nhome care amount that relates to home care subsidy that was or is\npayable in respect of 1 July 2015 or any later day.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nApplication and transitional provisions  Part 3\n\nNo. 19, 2016\nAged Care Legislation Amendment (Increasing Consumer Choice) Act",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nParagraph 46-1(1)(f) of the Aged Care Act 1997 and the Aged Care\n(Transitional Provisions) Act 1997, as inserted by this Schedule, applies\nin relation to any unspent home care amount that relates to home care\nsubsidy, and home care fees, that were or are payable in respect of\n1 July 2015 or any later day.\n(2)\nSubsection 95-1(3) of the Aged Care Act 1997, as inserted by this\nSchedule, applies in relation to any Commonwealth portion of unspent\nhome care amount that relates to home care subsidy that was or is\npayable in respect of 1 July 2015 or any later day.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nApplication and transitional provisions  Part 3\n\nNo. 19, 2016\nAged Care Legislation Amendment (Increasing Consumer Choice) Act",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016-sch-1-sec-79-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1f391212a1b970fdece9f72a151a0e1dec2849f32c7600d47ff1535edc65b6d4",
      "skos:note": "Applicability of Aged Care Act provisions to unspent home care amounts"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016#sch-1-sec-79",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "79 Unspent home care amount",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nParagraph 46-1(1)(f) of the Aged Care Act 1997 and the Aged Care\n(Transitional Provisions) Act 1997, as inserted by this Schedule, applies\nin relation to any unspent home care amount that relates to home care\nsubsidy, and home care fees, that were or are payable in respect of\n1 July 2015 or any later day.\n(2)\nSubsection 95-1(3) of the Aged Care Act 1997, as inserted by this\nSchedule, applies in relation to any Commonwealth portion of unspent\nhome care amount that relates to home care subsidy that was or is\npayable in respect of 1 July 2015 or any later day.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nApplication and transitional provisions  Part 3\n\nNo. 19, 2016\nAged Care Legislation Amendment (Increasing Consumer Choice) Act"
    },
